{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550304339,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799db8ffeuOxKeAZwQ1KPTs","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3888bd0001LcNecgRuwEn3Wj","sessionID":"ses_e2c799db8ffeuOxKeAZwQ1KPTs","messageID":"msg_1d38878e6001m3gmXtlR7zUIS0","type":"tool","id":"call_5e9671a7ce114b0797360c8c","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/scratch/live-heads.txt","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"Advisor: live; use sk-doc (needs a mode) 0.91/0.12 pass.\nAdvisor: prompt skipped.\nAdvisor: live; use system-skilled-doctor → /doctor:agents-md check (run) 0.80/0.26 pass.\n# Line 2 above is the task's exact prompt \"use the system-deep-loop skill\". The prompt policy skipped it:\n# shouldFireAdvisor returned {\"fire\":false,\"reason\":\"below_prompt_policy_threshold\",\"metalinguisticMentions\":[]},\n# where \"use the sk-doc skill\" returns {\"fire\":true,\"reason\":\"explicit_skill_or_governance_marker\",\"metalinguisticMentions\":[\"sk-doc\"]}.\n# The policy knows sk-* names as explicit skill markers and not system-* names. That file (prompt-policy.ts) is outside this phase.\n# Same check with a longer prompt, \"please use the system-deep-loop skill for this work\":\nAdvisor: live; use system-deep-loop (needs a mode) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n# And \"use the system-deep-loop skill on this packet\" gave:\nAdvisor: live; ambiguous: system-spec-kit 0.91/0.16 vs system-deep-loop 0.91/0.12 pass.\n\n# AFTER THE PROMPT POLICY FIX, 2026-11-13 (prompt-policy.ts now reads sk-, system-, cli- and mcp- skill names).\n# The task's three exact prompts, read through the worktree's own advisor daemon:\nAdvisor: live; use system-deep-loop (needs a mode) 0.91/0.12 pass.\nAdvisor: live; use sk-doc (needs a mode) 0.91/0.12 pass.\nAdvisor: live; use system-skilled-doctor → /doctor:agents-md check (run) 0.80/0.26 pass.\n# The same prompts with SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR set to a fresh folder while that daemon was running could not\n# start a second daemon, and the hook answered from the local fallback scorer:\n#   \"use the system-deep-loop skill\"  -> Advisor: stale; use system-deep-loop 0.95/0.15 pass.\n#   \"use the sk-doc skill\"            -> Advisor: stale; use sk-doc 0.95/0.15 pass.\n#   the doctor prompt                 -> Advisor: no skill matched.\n#   \"/create:readme for the utils folder\" -> Advisor: stale; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.95/0.15 pass.\n#   \"write a readme for the utils folder\" -> Advisor: stale; use system-spec-kit 0.95/0.20 pass.   (live: use sk-doc → /create:readme (start))\n# So the fallback path keeps a typed command and loses the mode label, the doctor hand-off and plain offers.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Advisor: live; use sk-doc (needs a mode) 0.91/0.12 pass.\nAdvisor: prompt skipped.\nAdvisor: live; use system-skilled-doctor → /doctor:agents-md check (run) 0.80/0.26 pass.\n# Line 2 above is the task's exact prompt \"use the system-deep-loop skill\". The prompt policy skipped it:\n# shouldFireAdvisor returned {\"fire\":false,\"reason\":\"below_prompt_policy_threshold\",\"metalinguisticMentions\":[]},\n# where \"use the sk-doc skill\" returns {\"fire\":true,\"reason\":\"explicit_skill_or_governance_marker\",\"metalinguisticMentions\":[\"sk-doc\"]}.\n# The policy knows sk-* names as explicit skill markers and not system-* names. That file (prompt-policy.ts) is outside this phase.\n# Same check with a longer prompt, \"please use the system-deep-loop skill for this work\":\nAdvisor: live; use system-deep-loop (needs a mode) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n# And \"use the system-deep-loop skill on this packet\" gave:\nAdvisor: live; ambiguous: system-spec-kit 0.91/0.16 vs system-deep-loop 0.91/0.12 pass.\n\n# AFTER THE PROMPT POLICY FIX, 2026-11-13 (prompt-policy.ts now reads sk-, system-, cli- and mcp- skill names).\n# The task's three exact prompts, read through the worktree's own advisor daemon:\nAdvisor: live; use system-deep-loop (needs a mode) 0.91/0.12 pass.\nAdvisor: live; use sk-doc (needs a mode) 0.91/0.12 pass.\nAdvisor: live; use system-skilled-doctor → /doctor:agents-md check (run) 0.80/0.26 pass.\n# The same prompts with SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR set to a fresh folder while that daemon was running could not\n# start a second daemon, and the hook answered from the local fallback scorer:\n#   \"use the system-deep-loop skill\"  -> Advisor: stale; use system-deep-loop 0.95/0.15 pass.\n#   \"use the sk-doc skill\"            -> Advisor: stale; use sk-doc 0.95/0.15 pass.\n#   the doctor prompt                 -> Advisor: no skill matched.\n#   \"/create:readme for the utils folder\" -> Advisor: stale; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.95/0.15 pass.\n#   \"write a readme for the utils folder\" -> Advisor: stale; use system-spec-kit 0.95/0.20 pass.   (live: use sk-doc → /create:readme (start))\n# So the fallback path keeps a typed command and loses the mode label, the doctor hand-off and plain offers.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cat specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/scratch/live-heads.txt\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550303696,"end":1794550304339}}}}
