ve `DIAG` with `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(process.cwd())` and record its line count, as in step 2 above -> 4. `bash: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"help me commit my changes\",\"cwd\":\"'\"$PWD\"'\",\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\"}' \\| SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1 node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/cl-001.stdout.json 2> /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/cl-001.shim-stderr.txt` -> 5. `bash: echo \"Exit: $?\"` -> 6. `bash: tail -n 1 \"$DIAG\"` -> 7. `bash:` pipe the same payload into `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` and capture its stderr | Exit code 0. Stdout is valid JSON and contains `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`. For a matching prompt it starts with `Advisor:` and a freshness word (`live` or `stale`). With no brief it starts with one of the three status lines: `Advisor: outage (`, `Advisor: no skill matched.` or `Advisor: prompt skipped.` `{}` means the shim failed, which is a FAIL. The shim's own stderr is empty. The diagnostics JSONL gains one line, and that record has `runtime: \"claude\"`, `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. The inner hook's stderr carries the same record shape. The raw prompt literal is absent from both | Preconditions:<br>`SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=UNSET`<br>`hook script exists`<br><br>Shim transcript, 2026-09-26, stdout ab...\n  Line 101: | No new diagnostics line | `AFTER` equals `BEFORE` | Confirm `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` reached the shim call and that `DIAG` resolved from the repository root. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts:\n  Line 320:   if (options.requireDebug !== false && !process.env.SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG) return;\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:\n  Line 81: 4. One hook adapter. The spec-kit shim never forwards its child's stderr, so read the skipped record from the diagnostics JSONL that `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` turns on:\n\n  Line 87:   | SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1 SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1 node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts:\n  Line 514:     const previousDebug = process.env.SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG;\n\n  Line 515:     process.env.SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG = '1';\n\n  Line 531:       if (previousDebug === undefined) delete process.env.SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG;\n\n  Line 532:       else process.env.SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG = previousDebug;\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v0.3.0.0.md:\n  Line 20: - **Diagnostic persistence is opt-in.** Advisor diagnostics previously flushed on every invocation, even when no one was reading them. `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` enables diagnostic record writes, while leaving it unset keeps diagnostic persistence disabled by default. Outcome records remain unconditional as part of the bounded-retention metrics contract.\n\n  Line 27: No migration required. On first invocation, the plugin discovers any pre-existing `~/.config/opencode/plugin/system-skill-advisor.json`. Set `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` if you want diagnostic records persisted. Leave it unset for the quiet default.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:\n  Line 147: `advisor_status` now carries `hookHealth`. It reports invocations, the p95 time, the fail-open rate and the cache-hit rate. The `/doctor:setup` advisor leg shows it. The hook writes these records only when `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set. So hook health shows only after such a run.\n\n  Line 253: - **If you want hook health in `/doctor:setup`:** run the hook once with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md:\n  Line 150: **Release validation.** `advisor_validate` runs the regression suite and reports threshold semantics (aggregate vs runtime) plus a prompt-safe `telemetry.outcomes.totals` block. Hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks so `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes. Records carry the runtime that served the turn, the bytes delivered (`emittedBytes`) and whether the directives were suppressed (`directivesSuppressed`). The code writes them only when `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set. The bounded trim writes a temp file and renames it over the log so a crash mid-trim keeps the old log.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md:\n  Line 42: Each record carries `runtime`, taken from `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` when it names a known runtime and `claude` otherwise. Records carry optional `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. The hook writes records only when `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set. Raw prompts never appear in diagnostics. Before exiting, the hook waits up to 100 ms for pending diagnostic writes.\n","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":26,"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 26 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs:\n  Line 300: // Gate verbose error/path logging behind SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG.\n\n  Line 303:   if (process.env.SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG === '1') {\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:\n  Line 294: - **If you run the skill advisor from a built copy:** ru