{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550462906,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799db8ffeuOxKeAZwQ1KPTs","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38acd1b001sh56wNg6V7G0ca","sessionID":"ses_e2c799db8ffeuOxKeAZwQ1KPTs","messageID":"msg_1d38ac3f4001lVsZOzH7qZcUhH","type":"tool","id":"call_b48513399403456ba15a4f2d","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - ux-cost-3 (UX and cost lane, segment three)\ndescription: Tracks the ux-cost-3 lineage of the segment-three command-surfacing research after phases 011, 012 and 013 are built: hook health default, brief token cost, cold start.\ntrigger_phrases: []\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n# Deep Research Strategy - ux-cost-3\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nLane label `ux-cost-3`: what the person and the model read, and what it costs, measured on the built state of phases 011, 012 and 013. Segment three of the command-surfacing research.\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nUX and cost lane. Two carried questions: (c) whether hook health should be written by default and at what byte, latency, growth and privacy cost, and (f) what the brief and the cold path cost per prompt now, plus any cut to the brief that loses no information. Anything already ranked, built or declined in segment one (`research/research.md`) or segment two (`research/research-segment-2.md` sections 3 and 4) is excluded unless a new measurement changes its disposition.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] KQ1: What should the hook-health default be, and what does a default-on record cost per prompt in bytes written, latency, file growth and privacy of what is recorded?\n- [ ] KQ2: What do the brief and the cold path cost per prompt at HEAD, and which brief bytes can be cut with the same command, policy and skill still reaching the model?\n- [ ] KQ3: Which ranked changes follow from the answers, by expected gain per unit of risk to the floors (typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, scorer [160,50,21,5])?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Re-recommending what phases 011, 012 and 013 built: typed delivery 44 of 44, the visibility guard, hook health in `advisor_status` and `/doctor:setup`, `measure-brief-cost.mjs`, the doctor hand-off naming, the `(needs a mode)` label, the deep pairs, the create anchors, the pointer write, the delivery leg, the OpenCode mapper fix.\n- Re-recommending segment-one and segment-two dispositions: trimming the comment-hygiene directive, the `create` rename, caching and precompute, keeping the embed model warm, warming the embedder at session start, raising the `COMMAND:` line rate, enriching intent signals (rank 15), the Gate 2 clause (operator).\n- Changing scorer weights, corpus labels, pins or the Python scorer.\n- Starting a model CLI session, an arena, an advisor daemon or ollama; running the full test suite.\n- Reading or printing the prompt text of a holdout row, or reading `holdout-prompts.jsonl`.\n- Editing any file outside this lineage directory.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence at newInfoRatio 0.05 or below, with every key question answered or explicitly carried forward.\n- Six iterations at most; a thin iteration is recorded with status `timeout` or `stuck`, not skipped.\n- Stop early only for unrecoverable state corruption or a missing control file.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n- none yet\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n- none yet\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n- none yet\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n- none yet\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 10. NEXT FOCUS\nKQ1: read the diagnostics writer and the `advisor_status` reader, then measure one debug-on record's bytes and the latency it adds to a hook invocation.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-3/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-3/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-3/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - ux-cost-3 (UX and cost lane, segment three)\\ndescription: Tracks the ux-cost-3 lineage of the segment-three command-surfacing research after phases 011, 012 and 013 are built: hook health default, brief token cost, cold start.\\ntrigger_phrases: []\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n# Deep Research Strategy - ux-cost-3\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\nLane label `ux-cost-3`: what the person and the model read, and what it costs, measured on the built state of phases 011, 012 and 013. Segment three of the command-surfacing research.\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nUX and cost lane. Two carried questions: (c) whether hook health should be written by default and at what byte, latency, growth and privacy cost, and (f) what the brief and the cold path cost per prompt now, plus any cut to the brief that loses no information. Anything already ranked, built or declined in segment one (`research/research.md`) or segment two (`research/research-segment-2.md` sections 3 and 4) is excluded unless a new measurement changes its disposition.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] KQ1: What should the hook-health default be, and what does a default-on record cost per prompt in bytes written, latency, file growth and privacy of what is recorded?\\n- [ ] KQ2: What do the brief and the cold path cost per prompt at HEAD, and which brief bytes can be cut with the same command, policy and skill still reaching the model?\\n- [ ] KQ3: Which ranked changes follow from the answers, by expected gain per unit of risk to the floors (typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, scorer [160,50,21,5])?\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Re-recommending what phases 011, 012 and 013 built: typed delivery 44 of 44, the visibility guard, hook health in `advisor_status` and `/doctor:setup`, `measure-brief-cost.mjs`, the doctor hand-off naming, the `(needs a mode)` label, the deep pairs, the create anchors, the pointer write, the delivery leg, the OpenCode mapper fix.\\n- Re-recommending segment-one and segment-two dispositions: trimming the comment-hygiene directive, the `create` rename, caching and precompute, keeping the embed model warm, warming the embedder at session start, raising the `COMMAND:` line rate, enriching intent signals (rank 15), the Gate 2 clause (operator).\\n- Changing scorer weights, corpus labels, pins or the Python scorer.\\n- Starting a model CLI session, an arena, an advisor daemon or ollama; running the full test suite.\\n- Reading or printing the prompt text of a holdout row, or reading `holdout-prompts.jsonl`.\\n- Editing any file outside this lineage directory.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Convergence at newInfoRatio 0.05 or below, with every key question answered or explicitly carried forward.\\n- Six iterations at most; a thin iteration is recorded with status `timeout` or `stuck`, not skipped.\\n- Stop early only for unrecoverable state corruption or a missing control file.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR: